  "id": "BIT-parse-2026-121965",
  "summary": "Parse Server before 8.6.113 and 9.10.6 Prototype Pollution via Dot Notation Key",
  "details": "Parse Server before 8.6.113 and 9.0.0 before 9.10.6 contains a prototype pollution vulnerability when building objects for Cloud Code triggers and LiveQuery, where a dot notation key whose intermediate segment resolves through an inherited member writes onto a process-wide built-in. Clients with write access to an object in a class with a trigger or LiveQuery can corrupt a built-in function, making unrelated requests fail until restart and denying service to all clients and hosted applications.",
